01:39.648 --> 01:42.818
- Yeah. That girl was mad.
- Yeah.

01:47.740 --> 01:49.575
Whose fault is that?

01:49.867 --> 01:51.243
Yours.

01:51.410 --> 01:54.204
Don't you feel guilty at all?

01:54.371 --> 01:57.958
Can't you be nice? Can't you be happy for your friend?

01:58.417 --> 02:01.211
I'd like to say the same thing to you.

02:01.378 --> 02:04.965
I didn't say you can't get a girlfriend.

02:06.508 --> 02:11.347
But, if you're going to get a girlfriend, be prepared to die.
That's all.

02:12.639 --> 02:13.932
Well put.

02:14.099 --> 02:16.101
We're best friends, right?

02:16.477 --> 02:18.145
These guys are crazy.

02:18.312 --> 02:19.605
Birds of a feather, right?

02:19.897 --> 02:20.939
Then...

02:22.191 --> 02:24.860
Then when are we ever going to get girlfriends?

02:26.445 --> 02:27.696
You're right.

02:28.072 --> 02:30.407
We spent too much time in your way.

02:30.741 --> 02:32.493
No. It's fine.

02:32.743 --> 02:34.161
It's fine?

02:34.328 --> 02:36.872
This is what an idiot once said:

02:37.039 --> 02:40.209
If one of us makes friends with them,
we can set up another mixer!

02:40.542 --> 02:43.921
You'll do it for us, right?
You're the guy with the girlfriend.

02:44.088 --> 02:47.257
Wait! Wait! Wait!
I already set up that mixer, right?

02:47.424 --> 02:49.009
I can't keep doing that!

02:49.635 --> 02:51.136
We'll pay 5000 yen per person.

02:51.428 --> 02:54.264
I'd be happy to help out a friend!

02:55.974 --> 02:59.478
So how can we get Chisa to accept?

02:59.645 --> 03:01.480
Who knows? I'm not involved.

03:01.647 --> 03:02.689
You'll get your share!

03:02.856 --> 03:04.858
We could get her to play a penalty game.

03:05.442 --> 03:06.860
I see.

03:07.236 --> 03:09.196
I guess we should do Truth or Dare.

03:09.363 --> 03:10.447
Something like that.

03:10.614 --> 03:14.618
The only problem will be getting Kotegawa to play.

03:14.785 --> 03:16.787
Well, I'll figure it out.

03:21.875 --> 03:23.001
Yeah.

03:23.210 --> 03:24.795
That should do it.

03:29.716 --> 03:31.301
Hey, you two.

03:32.136 --> 03:33.303
Would you like some?

03:33.846 --> 03:36.432
- Sashimi?
- Are you the one who cut it?

03:36.723 --> 03:39.059
Yeah. Can you taste it for me?

03:39.351 --> 03:40.519
Okay.

03:40.686 --> 03:42.938
You know how to cut fish?

03:47.109 --> 03:49.820
Truth or dare!

03:49.987 --> 03:51.572
Yeah!

03:52.781 --> 03:54.199
Hold on!

03:54.450 --> 03:56.577
Everyone has to draw one!

03:57.202 --> 03:58.579
One, two...

03:58.787 --> 03:59.913
Who's the king?

04:00.080 --> 04:01.623
All right! Stop!

04:01.790 --> 04:04.126
- What's wrong, Cakey?
- Why are you stopping us?

04:04.293 --> 04:05.586
Don't call me Cakey!

04:05.878 --> 04:07.296
Knock it off, Aina.

04:07.463 --> 04:09.381
If you draw, you have to play.

04:09.548 --> 04:12.468
He gave me this for the sashimi.

04:12.676 --> 04:13.844
What do you mean?

04:14.011 --> 04:16.221
Try remembering what Kitahara said just now.

04:17.514 --> 04:19.016
Would you like some?

04:19.892 --> 04:23.020
The word "sashimi" was never said, right?

04:23.187 --> 04:24.229
That was dirty!

04:24.855 --> 04:27.274
Don't be so mad, okay?

04:27.441 --> 04:30.486
Just try it once. You can quit if you don't like it.

04:31.403 --> 04:32.696
What do you want to do?

04:34.031 --> 04:35.491
Just once.

04:35.782 --> 04:38.160
Great! Let's try this again!

04:38.327 --> 04:40.454
Who's the king?

04:43.665 --> 04:44.875
It's me.

04:45.167 --> 04:47.628
- Give us your orders.
- Okay.

04:47.920 --> 04:50.881
Everyone except for me...

04:52.549 --> 04:54.843
has to keep playing until the end!

04:55.010 --> 04:56.261
- She got us.
- She got us.

04:56.553 --> 04:59.014
Why do you want us to play so badly?

04:59.640 --> 05:01.308
I wonder why...

05:01.475 --> 05:04.686
You have to obey the king's orders, Chisa-chan.

05:04.853 --> 05:06.396
You want us to play, too?

05:06.980 --> 05:10.400
You idiots! We've already bought those two out!

05:11.860 --> 05:12.903
A FEW HOURS EARLIER

05:13.195 --> 05:16.198
- Truth or dare?
- I see.

05:16.365 --> 05:17.407
What do you think?

05:18.033 --> 05:20.661
- Okay!
- I'm okay with it, too.

05:20.827 --> 05:22.037
Really?

05:23.080 --> 05:25.415
- You're so weird!
- Why are you so surprised?

05:25.582 --> 05:29.169
Well, I just thought you'd say no.

05:29.336 --> 05:30.420
PLAY TRICKS ON CHISA

05:30.587 --> 05:31.672
PLAY TRICKS ON NANAKA

05:34.299 --> 05:37.803
Well... Nothing bad will happen, right?

05:42.015 --> 05:43.934
Round two! Here we go!

05:44.434 --> 05:46.311
Who's the king?

05:46.603 --> 05:48.397
Oh, it's me again.

05:48.564 --> 05:49.940
Two in a row?

05:50.107 --> 05:51.400
You're good.

05:51.567 --> 05:57.447
Well, then... I order numbers 1 through 7
to take something off.

05:59.658 --> 06:01.702
You guys strip too fast!

06:01.994 --> 06:04.705
Come on, take it off, Nanaka!

06:07.583 --> 06:08.834
Okay...

06:10.127 --> 06:11.545
Stop!

06:11.712 --> 06:12.963
What's wrong, Aina?

06:13.130 --> 06:15.674
Taking off a sock is enough, right?

06:17.217 --> 06:18.844
I'll let you off this time.

06:19.136 --> 06:20.470
I see.

06:20.762 --> 06:23.515
No more dirty orders like that!

06:26.184 --> 06:28.103
Who's the king?

06:29.896 --> 06:31.565
It's me!

06:31.732 --> 06:33.066
What's your order?

06:33.233 --> 06:35.611
Nothing too crazy, okay?

06:36.236 --> 06:37.237
Okay!

06:37.404 --> 06:40.824
- Numbers 1 through 7...
- Yeah?

06:40.991 --> 06:43.118
can't strip at the next party!

06:44.578 --> 06:46.580
We have to obey...

06:46.747 --> 06:48.123
The king's orders.

06:48.415 --> 06:51.209
An order about wearing clothes? That's too crazy!

06:51.376 --> 06:52.502
You should be ashamed!

06:52.669 --> 06:55.130
Telling you to keep your clothes on isn't crazy!

06:55.297 --> 06:56.590
It can't be helped.

06:56.798 --> 06:59.176
We'll do our best to deal with it.

06:59.343 --> 07:01.011
Promise me, okay?

07:01.303 --> 07:03.013
Let's play the next round.

07:03.472 --> 07:05.390
Who's the king?

07:06.016 --> 07:07.267
It's me this time!

07:07.893 --> 07:10.103
Well, then... Number 3...

07:10.270 --> 07:11.271
I'm safe!

07:11.438 --> 07:16.526
Has to tell the person to the left
that she loves her sister!

07:17.152 --> 07:18.195
I get it...

07:18.362 --> 07:20.864
Hey. Don't be embarrassed. Say it.

07:21.031 --> 07:22.574
You're number 3, right?

07:22.741 --> 07:24.284
No, I'm not.

07:25.869 --> 07:28.789
Wait! Then who is--?

07:30.457 --> 07:31.792
It's me.

07:32.084 --> 07:33.335
This is wrong!

07:33.502 --> 07:36.046
This is going to be traumatic!

07:36.338 --> 07:38.131
- Sister...
- Shut up, Iori.

07:38.298 --> 07:40.884
You have to obey the king's orders, right?

07:41.468 --> 07:44.513
I love you, sister!

07:46.515 --> 07:48.433
Who's the king?

07:48.600 --> 07:49.726
Bad dreams...

07:49.893 --> 07:51.812
I'm going to have bad dreams about this.

07:52.813 --> 07:53.939
It's me!

07:55.357 --> 07:56.483
I got it, Kitahara!

07:56.650 --> 07:58.235
You did it, Kohei!

07:58.402 --> 08:01.071
All we have to do is find out what number Chisa drew.

08:02.447 --> 08:04.324
We rigged these chopsticks.

08:04.950 --> 08:08.704
The ones with unequal lengths are odd,
and the regular ones are even.

08:08.995 --> 08:13.959
The ones with round tips are in the first half,
and the square ones are the second half!

08:14.167 --> 08:15.961
Well...

08:16.253 --> 08:19.339
From the looks of those chopsticks,
Chisa is number 1 or number 3!

08:19.548 --> 08:21.883
Only two possibilities!
You can do it, Kohei!

08:22.050 --> 08:23.093
Okay!

08:23.635 --> 08:25.971
Kohei, give us your orders.

08:26.430 --> 08:32.978
Okay! I order you to introduce your friends
to the king at our next party!

08:34.354 --> 08:36.732
- Which number?
- Well, that's...

08:38.525 --> 08:39.860
Number 4!

08:41.319 --> 08:43.238
Why did you pick 4, you idiot?

08:43.405 --> 08:45.866
You held up four fingers!

08:46.033 --> 08:48.577
I tried to say Chisa is number 1 or 3, idiot!

08:48.744 --> 08:50.871
Those guys really were up to something.

08:52.456 --> 08:54.875
Okay, okay. That's enough fighting.

08:56.209 --> 08:58.628
- Oh, dear.
- Our plan failed.

08:58.920 --> 09:00.714
Don't be a sore loser.

09:00.881 --> 09:03.133
So, what were you trying to do?

09:03.759 --> 09:04.968
Our objective? Well...

09:05.135 --> 09:06.928
It's a long story.

09:07.095 --> 09:08.472
Make it short.

09:08.638 --> 09:10.265
Money and women.

09:10.432 --> 09:11.641
You guys are terrible.

09:11.933 --> 09:13.268
You're mistaken.

09:13.435 --> 09:16.396
Some guys promised us money
if we set up a mixer.

09:16.563 --> 09:19.775
This is a club activity to raise money for our trip.

09:20.192 --> 09:21.693
Oh, really?

09:21.860 --> 09:24.029
Why don't you try working again?

09:24.571 --> 09:26.239
It's hopeless.

09:26.406 --> 09:28.909
Too bad. Let's think of another way to get money.

09:29.075 --> 09:31.077
There's no time. We have to hurry.

09:31.244 --> 09:33.497
Choose something respectable this time.

09:33.663 --> 09:34.664
Yeah.

09:35.665 --> 09:37.918
- Wait, you two.
- What?

09:38.502 --> 09:41.546
We have to carry out the order just now.

09:48.595 --> 09:50.180
MEAT IZAKAYA
BULGING MUSCLES

09:50.472 --> 09:53.517
Hey! So you're the guys Tokita was talking about!

09:53.683 --> 09:55.936
You want to have a crazy party, right?

09:56.228 --> 09:58.438
Do you want to join our club?

09:58.730 --> 10:00.357
What's going on?

10:00.524 --> 10:02.234
We're not going to pay you for this!

10:02.400 --> 10:04.569
You should be paying us for this!

10:04.778 --> 10:07.113
Shut up! We did our best!

10:07.280 --> 10:09.825
You should pay us in recognition of our effort!

10:10.116 --> 10:13.954
No way!

10:17.999 --> 10:21.253
So do you have enough for the trip now?

10:21.419 --> 10:22.879
Not yet.

10:23.046 --> 10:24.548
I'm going to work tomorrow.

10:24.881 --> 10:26.925
It's a respectable job, right?

10:27.259 --> 10:30.178
We're going to be event staff. Azusa introduced us.

10:33.139 --> 10:34.391
Whoa, sounds hard.

10:34.558 --> 10:36.685
That's the only short-term job there was.

10:37.143 --> 10:40.939
- If you need money, how about coming?
- They're okay with you just showing up.

10:41.273 --> 10:43.817
- I'm going to decline.
- Me too.

10:44.150 --> 10:45.318
Hi!

10:45.652 --> 10:47.863
- Hey.
- All four of you came together?

10:48.029 --> 10:49.823
We ran into each other nearby.

10:50.156 --> 10:52.075
Radishes are so cheap.

10:52.242 --> 10:53.702
Nice.

10:54.244 --> 10:55.620
You need radishes?

10:55.787 --> 10:57.747
I was wondering what to do.

10:57.914 --> 10:59.416
We wanted one more.

10:59.583 --> 11:00.917
But it's over our budget.

11:01.084 --> 11:02.711
Then I'll go buy one.

11:04.963 --> 11:06.298
Well, that's...

11:06.464 --> 11:07.883
Don't worry about it.

11:08.049 --> 11:09.843
Well, you know...

11:10.010 --> 11:11.219
You're right.

11:11.553 --> 11:13.555
They're pretty expensive.

11:13.722 --> 11:16.099
How broke do they think I am?

11:16.433 --> 11:17.434
No...

11:17.601 --> 11:20.353
It's just one radish! I can afford it!

11:22.939 --> 11:24.524
Iori...

11:25.150 --> 11:26.401
Hey, Chii-chan.

11:26.568 --> 11:29.070
What are you going to do if Iori buys a radish?

11:34.117 --> 11:36.494
Fifteen minutes...

11:37.078 --> 11:40.206
I'll treat you like a human for fifteen minutes.

11:40.373 --> 11:41.625
Hear that, Iori?

11:41.791 --> 11:45.253
I wonder what she's been treating me like until now.

11:45.587 --> 11:48.131
But why do you want a radish?

11:49.799 --> 11:51.343
That's not it, Iori.

11:51.509 --> 11:54.137
We were talking about di-com, not daikon.

11:54.471 --> 11:55.972
- Di-com?
- Yeah.

11:56.139 --> 11:57.891
Dive computers.

11:58.141 --> 11:59.851
They cost about this much.

12:00.310 --> 12:02.270
You were going to make me buy this?

12:02.437 --> 12:05.273
I compromised as much as I could.

12:05.607 --> 12:08.026
Now that we're all here, let's go.

12:08.193 --> 12:09.194
Yeah.

12:09.361 --> 12:11.029
Where are we going?

12:12.238 --> 12:15.033
We're going to look at diving gear today.

12:19.037 --> 12:21.373
There's lots of different gear.

12:21.539 --> 12:24.292
I don't know what to look for.

12:24.626 --> 12:27.128
Is there something we should buy?

12:27.295 --> 12:29.965
They said rentals were okay in the beginning.

12:30.131 --> 12:32.175
That's what they told me too.

12:32.884 --> 12:35.261
I guess you need a towel and a swimsuit.

12:35.428 --> 12:37.222
A swimsuit?

12:37.389 --> 12:39.265
- Yeah!
- That's right!

12:39.474 --> 12:42.394
- All you need is a towel for now!
- I see.

12:42.560 --> 12:44.437
What about a swimsuit?

12:44.771 --> 12:48.108
When you buy your own gear,
you should start with a mask.

12:48.274 --> 12:49.317
Why?

12:49.484 --> 12:52.570
They're pretty cheap.

12:52.904 --> 12:56.866
The main purpose of diving
is to see what it looks like underwater.

12:57.033 --> 13:00.161
You don't want a mask that makes it hard to see.

13:00.328 --> 13:01.454
You're right.

13:01.788 --> 13:05.291
Some people say you should buy a dive computer first.

13:05.458 --> 13:10.839
They say you should get your own safety gear
to prevent decompression sickness.

13:11.172 --> 13:14.175
We've never worn dive computers before.

13:14.342 --> 13:16.052
Was that okay?

13:16.219 --> 13:17.971
Don't worry.

13:18.138 --> 13:20.849
You didn't dive to a dangerous depth.

13:21.057 --> 13:25.395
The instructors are careful not to let that happen.

13:25.562 --> 13:31.943
Divers who dive deep or swim far away
from their instructor need this gear.

13:34.529 --> 13:35.864
What's this?

13:36.031 --> 13:39.117
It's a reef hook.
You use it by hooking it.

13:39.576 --> 13:41.578
- What's this?
- It's a float.

13:41.745 --> 13:43.955
You put air in it and blow it up.

13:44.122 --> 13:45.248
I see.

13:46.750 --> 13:47.751
I'll save you!

13:51.838 --> 13:53.590
It's scary underwater.

13:53.757 --> 13:55.133
Yeah.

13:55.300 --> 13:58.136
That face... he's probably
thinking about something stupid.

13:58.803 --> 14:01.222
Have a look around.

14:01.389 --> 14:03.641
If you have any questions, just ask us.

14:03.975 --> 14:06.144
- Okay.
- Okay!

14:30.502 --> 14:32.045
What are you looking at?

14:32.420 --> 14:34.297
It's an unusual camera.

14:35.465 --> 14:37.675
You can take pictures like this.

14:37.842 --> 14:39.511
That is pretty unusual!

14:39.677 --> 14:41.054
It's interesting, right?

14:43.348 --> 14:44.974
Iori. Iori!

14:45.433 --> 14:47.560
- Hurry!
- What?

14:47.894 --> 14:51.064
- They also have these.
- What's that?

14:51.397 --> 14:53.775
It's a device for talking underwater.

14:53.942 --> 14:55.276
Seriously?

14:55.443 --> 14:57.445
It picks up sound through your bones.

14:57.612 --> 14:59.572
Modern science is amazing!

14:59.906 --> 15:02.700
There's a trick to talking through this.

15:03.034 --> 15:07.330
You're right. It's good to agree on the words in advance.

15:07.497 --> 15:09.916
It's hard to talk when you have a regulator on.

15:10.083 --> 15:12.710
Excuse me! I have a question.

15:12.877 --> 15:13.962
What's wrong?

15:14.129 --> 15:16.798
How do you choose a regulator?

15:16.965 --> 15:18.216
A regulator?

15:18.716 --> 15:20.885
You'll be fine with a rental.

15:21.052 --> 15:22.095
But...

15:22.929 --> 15:24.597
- In...
- In?

15:24.931 --> 15:27.058
It'll be an indirect kiss!

15:27.225 --> 15:29.686
Here's my regulator.

15:29.853 --> 15:32.647
Are you still worried about stuff like that?

15:32.814 --> 15:34.482
I've never thought about it before.

15:34.816 --> 15:37.735
You'll be fine. It's not an indirect kiss.

15:37.902 --> 15:42.657
- Really?
- Remember what it's like to hold the mouthpiece?

15:42.824 --> 15:44.951
You're right. It's not an indirect kiss.

15:45.118 --> 15:47.745
Right! It's more like...

15:48.079 --> 15:50.540
Use my toothbrush!

15:51.124 --> 15:52.959
It's like sharing a toothbrush!

15:53.126 --> 15:54.752
That's even worse!

15:55.086 --> 15:57.213
So, what really goes on?

15:57.380 --> 15:59.757
We disinfect them every day.

16:00.091 --> 16:03.887
If you're still worried about it,
you could kiss directly once.

16:04.053 --> 16:06.890
Actually, I was interested in indirect kissing.

16:07.056 --> 16:08.516
- You're terrible.
- Despicable.

16:08.850 --> 16:10.977
Forget about him. Let's look at swimsuits.

16:11.144 --> 16:13.646
You're right. Can I buy a new swimsuit?

16:13.980 --> 16:16.774
Did I say something wrong?

16:16.941 --> 16:18.151
Who knows.

16:20.486 --> 16:22.280
By the way, Kotegawa...

16:22.447 --> 16:25.158
- You can just call me Chisa.
- Then you can call me Aina.

16:25.491 --> 16:28.661
- I wanted to ask you.
- What?

16:30.288 --> 16:32.624
Are you going out with Iori?

16:41.090 --> 16:43.176
Your face gave me the answer.

16:44.010 --> 16:46.512
Then what was that about at the Izu Spring Festival?

16:46.679 --> 16:50.308
The beauty pageant was a lot of trouble. That's why...

16:54.145 --> 16:56.689
- In the first place--
- Sir!

16:57.482 --> 16:59.609
Please change in the changing room!

16:59.776 --> 17:01.486
Sorry, it's not our habit.

17:01.653 --> 17:04.113
Hey, don't change in the hallway.

17:04.280 --> 17:05.698
Your clothes are in the way!

17:05.865 --> 17:07.825
That's not the problem!

17:07.992 --> 17:11.829
- I could never imagine going out with him.
- You're right.

17:12.288 --> 17:14.123
What happened to Kohei?

17:14.290 --> 17:15.708
Yeah. I haven't seen him.

17:15.875 --> 17:17.335
I'll go find him.

17:19.587 --> 17:21.339
Oh, there he is.

17:26.010 --> 17:28.054
- What are you doing?
- Kitahara!

17:28.221 --> 17:30.098
So you were lead here too?

17:30.265 --> 17:32.475
No, I was just looking for you.

17:33.142 --> 17:35.687
- You want a wetsuit?
- I wasn't planning on buying one,

17:35.853 --> 17:37.105
but I want this one!

17:37.272 --> 17:39.232
You're right. It's a unique design.

17:40.650 --> 17:41.901
What's gotten into you?

17:42.193 --> 17:44.988
Kitahara, don't you know what anime this is from?

17:45.196 --> 17:47.365
You can't try it on in that size.

17:47.532 --> 17:50.535
No! I don't have to be the one to wear it!

17:51.119 --> 17:52.787
Oh, I see.

17:52.954 --> 17:55.540
We can ask someone who fits how it feels.

17:56.291 --> 17:57.333
I didn't mean--

17:57.500 --> 17:58.501
Hey!

18:06.175 --> 18:08.219
Yeah. It feels good.

18:08.386 --> 18:11.723
It doesn't have a zipper. Some people might not like it.

18:11.889 --> 18:13.266
Hear that, Kohei?

18:19.272 --> 18:23.318
I'm going to call you my best friend just for today.

18:23.484 --> 18:25.153
What? That's creepy.

18:27.447 --> 18:29.657
Well, what are you going to do?

18:29.907 --> 18:31.951
I can't buy it now, but someday...

18:32.118 --> 18:34.412
That was a woman's wetsuit.

18:34.746 --> 18:35.913
How was it?

18:36.247 --> 18:37.874
Is there anything you want?

18:38.041 --> 18:40.209
There was a lot of stuff.

18:40.376 --> 18:43.129
I'm going to get a mask like you recommended.

18:43.296 --> 18:45.798
- What about you, Aina?
- I'll get a mask too.

18:45.965 --> 18:47.925
MASK 9,500 YEN

18:48.092 --> 18:49.802
MASK 8,820 YEN

18:58.353 --> 19:00.563
Hey, Chisa. How do I choose a mask?

19:06.194 --> 19:09.530
- Chisa...
- Chii-chan's so cute!

19:09.697 --> 19:11.324
Youth! It's youth!

19:11.491 --> 19:12.867
What are you talking about?

19:13.034 --> 19:17.080
She's so cute looking at cameras.

19:17.413 --> 19:20.041
Maybe she just wants to take a picture to celebrate.

19:20.208 --> 19:21.209
That's why.

19:22.377 --> 19:28.174
She's probably happy that she made friends her age
she can go diving with.

19:29.050 --> 19:32.470
She really loves diving, doesn't she?

19:32.637 --> 19:34.222
That's right.

19:34.389 --> 19:37.225
GRAND BLUE

19:38.601 --> 19:39.977
We're back.

19:40.144 --> 19:41.229
Welcome back!

19:44.315 --> 19:46.859
- You guys bought a lot!
- Yeah.

19:47.193 --> 19:48.861
We bought masks.

19:49.028 --> 19:50.279
I bought a camera.

19:50.446 --> 19:52.365
Wow, you guys worked hard.

19:53.032 --> 19:54.033
Worked hard?

19:54.200 --> 19:56.244
We just went shopping.

19:57.703 --> 19:59.122
That's not what I mean.

19:59.288 --> 20:03.000
Going to Okinawa is expensive.
And you even bought new gear!

20:05.169 --> 20:07.004
FESTIVAL 2018

20:17.348 --> 20:19.308
Please have a look!

20:19.475 --> 20:21.602
Have a look...

20:26.357 --> 20:27.775
Hey, Kitahara...

20:28.109 --> 20:30.361
When do we go on break?

20:30.528 --> 20:32.905
We just started a few minutes ago.

20:33.239 --> 20:34.490
Hey, Kitahara.

20:34.657 --> 20:37.493
Shut up. I'm going to kill you.

20:38.619 --> 20:40.288
GRAND BLUE

20:41.831 --> 20:43.541
I can't get married anymore!

20:43.708 --> 20:45.835
You'll be fine! Yes you can!

20:46.002 --> 20:47.920
What's she crying about?

20:48.087 --> 20:50.423
We're naked almost every day.

20:54.427 --> 20:57.263
OKINAWA

21:03.019 --> 21:05.313
I'll do a license class over there.

21:05.480 --> 21:07.940
Then me and Kotobuki will go every other day.

21:08.107 --> 21:09.275
Okay!

21:10.109 --> 21:15.656
After making lots of preparations,
the time finally came for our Okinawa trip!

21:18.451 --> 21:19.702
Hey, you guys!

21:20.536 --> 21:22.455
We've arrived in Okinawa!

21:22.705 --> 21:26.209
Yeah!

21:28.044 --> 21:29.796
Here. This is yours, Aina.

21:29.962 --> 21:31.964
No!

21:33.841 --> 21:35.927
Here's your mic, Kitahara.

21:36.135 --> 21:39.972
Me too? All right, let's do this!

21:40.264 --> 21:43.726
- Yeah, sing your heart out.
- You guys seem to be having fun.

21:45.144 --> 21:51.150
A fairytale whispers
In a fake world

21:51.317 --> 21:57.073
Hiding in the complete darkness

21:57.240 --> 22:03.037
I reach for the forbidden fruit
In my last days

22:03.204 --> 22:09.293
Now I know the meaning of the song about hope

22:09.585 --> 22:14.590
A broken gear will never stop again

22:14.757 --> 22:22.181
Even if I were to lose everything
I'd still want you to know

22:22.348 --> 22:28.396
Trapped in the sky so far away
I'm praying with ripped off wings

22:28.604 --> 22:34.235
Because we span together
The vows of arpeggio

22:34.402 --> 22:40.157
If life sparkles only to the beat
Of the resonating stars

22:40.324 --> 22:43.160
I'll sacrifice everything

22:43.327 --> 22:47.915
Till death do us apart

22:48.124 --> 22:50.001
Cheers!

22:54.672 --> 22:57.216
Previews are coming up next!

23:02.930 --> 23:04.682
It's so warm!

23:05.016 --> 23:07.393
It's a tropical island!

23:07.727 --> 23:09.312
Cheers!

23:10.104 --> 23:11.564
BUT... HOWEVER...

23:13.899 --> 23:16.319
Is this a rip current?

23:16.485 --> 23:19.113
I told you not to underestimate the sea!

23:19.280 --> 23:21.198
THEY WERE SWEPT AWAY
BY A RIP CURRENT DURING CLASS

23:21.449 --> 23:24.201
ON A DESERTED ISLAND

23:26.245 --> 23:27.872
Let's go, Iori.

23:28.039 --> 23:30.666
You can't cry about it forever.

23:30.833 --> 23:35.838
No! I can't leave his dead body here!

23:36.631 --> 23:38.507
He's my best friend!

23:39.050 --> 23:41.218
My first, and last...

23:41.761 --> 23:44.221
THE DEATH OF A FRIEND.
IT HAS NO MEANING.

23:45.014 --> 23:46.849
AND A MAN-EATING SHARK APPEARS.

23:47.516 --> 23:49.977
What should we do about that man-eating shark?

23:50.144 --> 23:52.021
What a pain.

23:52.188 --> 23:55.608
Why don't we lure it in with Kohei's corpse?

23:55.858 --> 23:58.611
CAN IORI AND THE OTHERS SURVIVE!?

23:59.195 --> 24:00.196
Grand Blue Dreaming

24:00.363 --> 24:01.947
DEPENDING ON CIRCUMSTANCES, THE
PRESENTATION, ACTING, AND CONTENT MAY DIFFER.

24:06.661 --> 24:09.038
We can stretch out in this room.

24:09.288 --> 24:12.500
We have to rest well for the class.

24:12.750 --> 24:14.043
Goodnight!

24:14.210 --> 24:15.461
Goodnight!

24:15.628 --> 24:16.962
NEXT EPISODE
"ARRIVAL IN OKINAWA"
